    "summary": "Not built as asked — do not mount a shelf for glass jars and books directly above a baby's cot. Anything stored overhead can fall onto the baby, and glass can shatter; 3D-printed plastic wall fixings here have no verified load rating, child-safety, or earthquake/tug resistance. Safe alternative: mount any nursery shelf on a different wall well away from the cot and out of the baby's reach, never store glass jars over or near the cot (use shatterproof containers inside closed storage instead), choose a low, securely wall-anchored shelf with a retaining lip for books only, and have mounting checked by a qualified installer. If you want, I can build a book-only shelf designed for a wall away from the cot."
